# A permanent may have several Roles if each is controlled by a different player (CR 704.5z, the Role rulings). Bot2's
# Royal Treatment gives its Ornithopter Bot2's Royal Role. On Bot1's next turn a kicked Thieving Skydiver takes the
# Ornithopter: its enters trigger targets Bot2's creature, whose ward {1} triggers for Bot1, who pays it (CR 702.21a).
# The Role stays Bot2's (CR 303.4e). Then Bot1's own Royal Treatment on its new Ornithopter makes a Royal Role Bot1
# controls: two Roles on one creature, of two controllers, so neither goes - the Ornithopter is a 2/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Thieving Skydiver
Royal Treatment
Island
Forest
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Ornithopter
Royal Treatment
Forest x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Royal Treatment.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thieving Skydiver.Cast(Kicked: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.PayCost
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Royal.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Royal Treatment.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

